Built and locally verified the Track B generator, but it is not submission-ready because OpenRouter quota prevented completing the mandatory oracle loop.

- Module: [gen_2504_18390.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2504.18390/gen_2504_18390.py:33)
- Local results: [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2504.18390/selftest_report.json)
- Current oracle evidence: [llm_loop_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2504.18390/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- Full handoff: [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2504.18390/README.md:3)

Key results:

- All local G1–G9(c) gates pass.
- Independent expansion produced 525 blocks covering all 7,875 point pairs exactly once.
- Exact shipping density: `1 / 11,019,960,576`.
- Four attacks: `0/8` successes each.
- Track B reference algorithm: 4,754 operations; compact invariant route: 98 operations.
- Answer size: 175 characters, 48 atoms.
- Two scored oracles solved `easy`; five subsequent calls received HTTP 403 total-limit errors. No `medium`/`hard` verdict was obtained.
- G9 arms remain unscored for the same reason.

The [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.18390) is a fixed-order catalogue without a scalable hardness theorem, so Track A would be unjustified. I did not create `REJECTED.md`: the family passes G/H/V locally, and the remaining blocker is external quota.
